\subsection{D1: Distance Between Barycenter and Random Vertex}
\textbf{Purpose:} The D1 Shape Distribution measures how an object's shape spreads out and how its points are arranged around its centre.

\textbf{Calculation:}
\begin{align*}
b &= \text{barycenter of all vertices}\\
d_i &= \| v_i - b \|, \quad i = 1, \dots, N
\end{align*}
Collect all $d_i$ into a histogram with 10 bins to form descriptor $D_1$.

\textbf{Proof:} Figure~4.0 shows that round objects have a narrow peak (uniform distance to centre), while elongated shapes have a wider distribution.

