\end{figure}

\subsection{A3: Angle Between 3 Random Vertices}
\textbf{Purpose:} The A3 Shape Distribution examines how the angles between triplets of random points on an object's surface vary, revealing shape smoothness or irregularity.

\textbf{Calculation:}
\[
\theta = \arccos \left( \frac{a \cdot b}{\|a\| \|b\|} \right)
\]
where $a = v_1 - v_2$ and $b = v_3 - v_2$. Collect $N=10{,}000$ such angles into a histogram.

\textbf{Proof:} Figure~4.1 shows that flat models have peaks at lower angles, while round shapes show broader distributions.

