\subsection{D2: Distance Between 2 Random Vertices}
\textbf{Purpose:} The D2 descriptor characterises a shape based on the distribution of Euclidean distances between random vertex pairs.

\textbf{Calculation:}
\[
d_k = \| v_{i_k} - v_{j_k} \|, \quad k = 1, \dots, N
\]
All distances are binned into a histogram of 10 bins.

\textbf{Proof:} Figure~4.2 shows that round and flat shapes have consistent distance peaks, while elongated and irregular ones have broader distributions.

