\subsection{D3: Square Root of Triangle Area Formed by 3 Random Vertices}
\textbf{Purpose:} The D3 descriptor analyses geometric relationships between three vertices by computing the square root of the triangle area they form.

\textbf{Calculation:}
\begin{align*}
a &= \| v_2 - v_1 \|, \quad b = \| v_3 - v_2 \|, \quad c = \| v_1 - v_3 \| \\
s &= \frac{a + b + c}{2} \\
A_\triangle &= \sqrt{s (s - a) (s - b) (s - c)}
\end{align*}
All $\sqrt{A_\triangle}$ values are collected into a histogram.

\textbf{Proof:} Figure~4.3 shows that round shapes have a narrow central peak, while elongated and irregular shapes have broader distributions.

