\subsection{D4: Cube Root of Volume of Tetrahedron Formed by 4 Random Vertices}
\textbf{Purpose:} The D4 descriptor quantifies volumetric properties of shapes by analysing tetrahedral volumes formed by four random points.

\textbf{Calculation:}
\begin{align*}
a &= v_2 - v_1, \quad b = v_3 - v_1, \quad c = v_4 - v_1 \\
V &= \frac{1}{6} | a \cdot (b \times c) |
\end{align*}
To stabilise the feature, the cube root of $V$ is used, and all values are binned into 10 histogram bins.

\textbf{Proof:} Figure~4.4 shows similar curves across shapes, with flatter shapes skewed toward lower volumes as expected.


